    RESIDUE, DISCLOSED AND BOUNDED BY AAP SECTION 0.3.2
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Enabling `display_grid` gives assistive technology a correct route to
    the values; it does NOT rewrite the per-point description. After the
    change the bars still announce the same "100.0%" strings
    (re-measured on the rendered page: unchanged, byte for byte), and the
    screen-reader information region is unchanged ("Bar chart with
    6 bars." / "The chart has 1 Y axis displaying Case Count.
    Range: 0 to 8." / "End of interactive chart."). Two further measured
    caveats: the grid declares no `role` and no caption, so it is
    announced as an unlabeled table adjacent to the chart; and it sits
    below the chart inside the widget's `overflow:auto` body (client
    height 305px vs scroll height 538px), so a sighted user must scroll
    within the widget to see it and no chart-vs-grid toggle exists.

    Correcting the announcement itself requires changing
    `accessibility.point.valueDescriptionFormat` for column series, which
    lives in the platform's own charting bundle
    (GlideV2ChartingIncludes.jsx / chart_includes.cssx): a GLOBAL
    artifact. AAP Section 0.3.2 verbatim prohibits
        "Global scope changes of any kind"
    and AAP Section 0.7.2 verbatim requires
        "Scope-namespace exclusivity ... zero global-scope writes are
         permitted."
    No scoped `sys_report` column overrides the point-description
    template on this release: `custom_config` (max_length 5000) is used
    only for chart `transforms` in every out-of-the-box row,
    `style_config` is empty on every report on the instance,
    `show_chart_total` is enabled by zero of the 182 bar reports, and the
    widget's Highcharts context menu offers only "Save as PNG" and "Save
    as JPEG" (no "View data table" item). The remaining defect is
    therefore bounded by the AAP Section 0.3.2 exception: it is reported,
    not worked around.

