    THE SECOND IN-SCOPE REMEDY APPLIED
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    <show_chart_data_label>true</show_chart_data_label>

    Measured on the committed row before this change, this report shipped
    `show_chart_data_label = false` - so the only place the real category
    value existed was a hover tooltip and the data grid, and the grid is
    below the fold of the widget's scrolling body. `show_chart_data_label`
    is a stock `sys_report` boolean (column label "Show chart data
    label", sys_dictionary default `false`, hence OFF when the element is
    omitted) that turns on Highcharts data labels for the series. With it
    enabled each bar carries its own COUNT as persistent on-canvas text
    next to the bar - the real category value, painted once per point,
    with no hover and no scrolling required. Precedent on this instance:
    4 of the 182 `type=bar` reports already ship it enabled, so it is a
    supported report option and not a platform modification, which keeps
    the remedy inside AAP Section 0.3.2. The chart type is untouched -
    <type>bar</type> is still mandated verbatim by AAP Section 0.4.4
    ("bar chart for 'All cases by status'") and Section 0.5.1 ("Bar
    grouped by status").

    NAMED OPEN LIMITATION 1: PER-POINT PERCENTAGE ANNOUNCED AS 100.0%
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    STATUS: OPEN. Not mitigated, not "acceptable", not "close enough",
    and not "more accessible than before" - the defect QA Issue 11
    describes is still present after this change and is recorded as
    outstanding.

      - WHAT ASSISTIVE TECHNOLOGY SAYS (verbatim, measured per point):
            "1. Draft, 4, 100.0%"        "2. Closed, 2, 100.0%"
            "3. In Progress, 2, 100.0%"  "4. Open, 2, 100.0%"
            "5. Resolved, 2, 100.0%"     "6. Pending, 1, 100.0%"
      - WHAT IT SHOULD SAY: the category's share of the report total -
            "1. Draft, 4, 30.8%" · "2. Closed, 2, 15.4%" · … ·
            "6. Pending, 1, 7.7%" - i.e. the same shares the tooltip and
            the data grid already print correctly.
      - WHY NO IN-SCOPE RECORD SETTING CHANGES IT: the string is built by
        the platform's Highcharts wrapper from
        `accessibility.point.valueDescriptionFormat =
         "{index}. {point.name}, {point.y}, {point.percentage:.1f}%"`,
        and `point.percentage` is computed per STACK. ServiceNow renders
        each category of a single-series bar report as its own stack, so
        `point.total === point.y` and `point.percentage === 100` for
        every bar by construction. `sys_report.compute_percent` cannot
        redirect it: its active sys_choice list on this release offers
        exactly two values, `aggregate` ("Use Aggregation") and `count`
        ("Use Record Count") - both of which select WHICH aggregate a
        percentage is taken of, not how a point's own percentage is
        computed or announced. No other column on `sys_report` carries a
        point-description template: `custom_config` holds only chart
        `transforms` in every out-of-box row, `style_config` is empty on
        every report on this instance, and the `legend_*` / axis columns
        touch presentation only.
      - WHAT A HUMAN WOULD HAVE TO AUTHORISE: an edit to the platform's
        own charting bundle (GlideV2ChartingIncludes.jsx /
        chart_includes.cssx) or an equivalent global accessibility
        override, so that column series compute the percentage against
        the report total rather than the per-point stack. That is a
        GLOBAL, out-of-application change, and AAP Section 0.3.2 verbatim
        prohibits "Global scope changes of any kind" while AAP Section
        0.7.2 verbatim requires "zero global-scope writes are permitted".
        It is therefore reported for human decision, not worked around.

    NAMED OPEN LIMITATION 2: THE FALLBACK GRID IS UNLABELLED AND BELOW
    THE FOLD
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    STATUS: OPEN. Measured: the `table.chart_legend.display-grid-table`
    the `display_grid` remedy renders declares no `role` and carries no
    `<caption>`, so it is announced as an unlabelled table adjacent to
    the chart; and it sits below the chart inside the widget's
    `overflow:auto` body (client height 305px against scroll height
    538px), so reaching it means scrolling INSIDE the widget, with no
    chart-vs-grid toggle offered - the widget's Highcharts context menu
    exposes only "Save as PNG" and "Save as JPEG", no "View data table"
    item. Both the caption/role and the grid's placement are emitted by
    the same global chart component; nothing on the `sys_report` record
    or on the dashboard's `sys_portal_preferences` supplies a caption, a
    `role`, a toggle or a different insertion point. Same AAP Section
    0.3.2 / Section 0.7.2 boundary as Limitation 1, same disposition:
    reported for human authorisation, OPEN.

    Both limitations are carried forward in ../docs/dashboards.md so they
    survive outside this file's header.

